ozTTgemm: Ozaki I/II GEMM for Tenstorrent Blackhole

This distribution contains an independent, adapted copy of the calculation code of
the authors' research repository (not public; paper-data snapshot, revision
63e84a6c179bcf3e2865fb04e82b756aab55d3d6). The host interface, library build, and
execution entry points were written for standalone use. All library source files carry
Apache-2.0 SPDX identifiers. The directory experiments/ is a verbatim copy of the
research programs, scripts and measurement logs at the same snapshot (Apache-2.0; most
of its source files carry the SPDX identifier, the rest are covered by this notice).
See ORIGIN.md for what was taken and changed, and SOURCE_MAP.tsv for the original
files and their SHA-256 values.

Files derived from TT-Metalium (Copyright (c) 2023 Tenstorrent USA, Inc., Apache-2.0):
the matmul kernel src/backend/common/kernels/bmm_int32_spill.cpp is a modified copy of
tt-metal's bmm_large_block_zm.cpp; in experiments/, src/common/kernels/bmm_int32_spill.cpp
(the same kernel), src/common/kernels/bmm_l1acc.cpp, src/baseline/gemm_bf16.cpp and
src/baseline/gemm_bf16ext.cpp are derived from tt-metal's matmul kernels and examples.

TT-Metalium and its dependencies are otherwise external components, distributed
separately under their respective licenses. Their source and binaries are not bundled
here.
